<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>Breaking news from AFRICA, Maghreb and Sub-Saharan Africa - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of events, politics and social issues across Africa, including North Africa (the Maghreb) and the Sahel, aided by our network of correspondents and experts across the continent.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 16:05:56 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Tunisia water crisis deepens as temperatures approach 50°C</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-tunisia-water-crisis-deepens-as-temperatures-approach-50%C2%B0c</link><description>
In Tunisia, powerful heatwaves are driving power cuts and water shortage. While the country has been dealing with structural water scarcity and recurring drought for years, the current crisis is fuelling anger against the government, even as authorities attempt to coordinate water distribution efforts to quell the crisis. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1565123a-9d21-11f1-a401-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-20T193544Z-1767851294-RC2J2NAOH5H8-RTRMADP-3-TUNISIA-POLITICS-PROTESTS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1565123a-9d21-11f1-a401-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-20T193544Z-1767851294-RC2J2NAOH5H8-RTRMADP-3-TUNISIA-POLITICS-PROTESTS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9e48d1b2-a795-11f1-8dfd-d5757aa94ac8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 13:52:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Kenyan editor found safe after abduction</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/kenyan-editor-found-safe-after-abduction</link><description>
In tonight's edition: Media rights groups in Kenya call for an investigation after a top journalist is abducted overnight by heavily armed men. Also, trials for three potential vaccines against the Bundibugyo strain of Ebola are due to start over the next couple of months. Plus Senegalese consumers who are frustrated by the rising cost of living have launched a new campaign. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1de302e-a775-11f1-8a63-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-14106867926a9936eaaff518-88132835.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1de302e-a775-11f1-8a63-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-14106867926a9936eaaff518-88132835.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c6b02712-a70a-11f1-a83d-b37d75498e93</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 20:15:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Spanish report flags Moroccan police's 'total permissiveness' in Ceuta migrant rush</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260902-spanish-report-flags-moroccan-police-s-total-permissiveness-in-ceuta-migrant-rush</link><description>
Moroccan security forces displayed "total permissiveness" during last month's massive wave of migrants who crossed into the Spanish North African territory of Ceuta, according to a Spanish police report seen by a French news agency on Wednesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0cf6d932-a517-11f1-b815-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26233420530465.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0cf6d932-a517-11f1-b815-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26233420530465.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1ffac56a-a702-11f1-a811-33773faa09bf</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 19:20:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0cf6d932-a517-11f1-b815-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26233420530465.jpg">© Antonio Sempere, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>IMF reaches historical loan agreement with Senegal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/imf-reaches-historical-loan-agreement-with-senegal</link><description>
The IMF and Senegal have agreed on a new 2.2 billion-dollar loan programme to support financial reforms, a relief for the country after a huge amount of unreported debt recently came to light. The president has accused his predecessor of hiding the true state of the country's imbalanced budget deficit.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3ec4acbc-a6cc-11f1-8756-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-13096693496a981a859ef385-37983370.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3ec4acbc-a6cc-11f1-8756-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-13096693496a981a859ef385-37983370.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">23216ce0-a6b1-11f1-8e1d-eb672b3e2093</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 12:51:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Kenya shifts to electric cars as fuel prices soar 50%</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-kenya-shifts-to-electric-cars-as-fuel-prices-soar-50</link><description>
In Kenya, locally made eletric vehicles are gaining traction as fuel prices rise. As more and more Kenyans consider going electric, local firms are stepping up to assemble EV's domestically. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/801b0504-a6b7-11f1-b665-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1348699306a97f7b7ead947-66020292.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/801b0504-a6b7-11f1-b665-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1348699306a97f7b7ead947-66020292.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">227b7832-a6b4-11f1-8fd4-97aa81b9fddf</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 11:19:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Illegal mining ravages Johannesburg neighbourhoods</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-illegal-mining-ravages-johannesburg-neighbourhoods</link><description>
Some houses in one Johannesburg neighbourhood are in danger of collapse because of illegal mining. Known as Zama Zamas, around 34,000 illegal miners are thought to be working in South Africa, in the hope of finding gold and chromium. The mines they dig hollow out the ground, which causes buildings to collapse as well as frequent power outages.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/979dd432-a6b6-11f1-8180-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-21356417506a97f631c90f48-96540535.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/979dd432-a6b6-11f1-8180-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-21356417506a97f631c90f48-96540535.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4b32d776-a6b3-11f1-9a33-97aa81b9fddf</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 11:14:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Military buildup seen in Ethiopia near Sudanese border</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-military-buildup-seen-in-ethiopia-near-sudanese-border</link><description>
A major military buildup has been observed on the Ethiopian side of the Sudanese border. It comes amid intensified fighting between the Sudanese armed forces and the Rapid Support Forces (RSF). Sudan and Ethiopia have both accused each other of supporting rebels within their borders.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f7430e9e-9170-11f1-ae5d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26105668493216.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f7430e9e-9170-11f1-ae5d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26105668493216.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d1c0de36-a6af-11f1-bd07-97aa81b9fddf</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 10:57:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>South Africans missing in Nepal's glacial flood</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/south-africans-missing-in-nepal-s-glacial-flood</link><description>
In tonight's edition: Africa Disaster Relief is looking for six South Africans who went missing in the deadly floods on the border between Nepal and China. Also, South African illegal miners are undermining their own communities. Finally, rising fuel prices are pushing Kenyans towards electric vehicles. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/790c65f8-a6a5-11f1-ac73-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-10305230806a97d979116d37-48815514.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/790c65f8-a6a5-11f1-ac73-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-10305230806a97d979116d37-48815514.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3458c14c-a644-11f1-93c3-6de1e843c926</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 20:35:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Niger's thwarted mutiny highlights junta's dependence on Russia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260901-what-russia-helping-niger-junta-stop-mutiny-means-for-its-sovereignty</link><description>
A failed mutiny in Niger over the weekend shows how important Russia's Africa Corps mercenaries are in the country, according to analysts. They argue that the failed mutiny on Saturday shows how the country's security landscape has worsened and contradicts claims from Niger's junta about the country's independence from foreign powers. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3dee046c-a610-11f1-ab0a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36LJ3WE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3dee046c-a610-11f1-ab0a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36LJ3WE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c1254274-a60f-11f1-9f90-afc18f454785</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 15:16:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3dee046c-a610-11f1-ab0a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36LJ3WE.jpg">© Yuri Kochetkov, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ghana cocoa farmers reject new 'punitive' land conversion law</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-ghana-cocoa-farmers-reject-new-punitive-land-conversion-law</link><description>
Ghanaian cocoa farmers are ramping up their pushback against a new law preventing them from using their land for anything else without permission. President Mahama says supporting local processing is the key to economic growth. Cocoa chiefs say that the changes still leave the sector resting on an outdated colonial model.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66e10e78-90a8-11f1-b54b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26066850241444.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66e10e78-90a8-11f1-b54b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26066850241444.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">84c2b0ce-a5eb-11f1-aa0b-53703fbaf52c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 14:05:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>DR Congo's opposition rejects president's dialogue offer and calls for demonstration</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-dr-congo-s-opposition-rejects-president-s-dialogue-offer-and-calls-for-demonstration</link><description>
In DR Congo, managing the spread of Ebola is made all the more difficult as the country is juggling simultaneous security crises including untangling a peace deal with M23 rebels. President Felix Tshisekedi offered to convene a national dialogue which opposition parties call a smoke screen hiding an attempted power grab.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f3eb084-a60a-11f1-87d6-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26163611421863.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f3eb084-a60a-11f1-87d6-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26163611421863.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">85ce0d0a-a5e7-11f1-8c92-530b91485ab7</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 13:40:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>As capital goes back to normal, Niger downplays soldiers' mutiny</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-as-capital-goes-back-to-normal-niger-downplays-soldiers-mutiny</link><description>
Niger's capital is back to normal after an intense week-end. A soldier mutiny took over Niamey on August 29, which was stopped by the army alongside the Russian paramilitary Africa Corps. The next day, Algeria sent four fighters aircrafts and two other military planes as cooperation with Nigeria is recently back on : an unexpected decision. Since it got independence, Algeria's non intervention doctrine is part of its DNA. FRANCE 24's Harold Girard tells us more about the goal of this decision.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68cf32c8-a5f2-11f1-980b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-30T193523Z-1134131169-RC259NAMFZV1-RTRMADP-3-NIGER-SECURITY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68cf32c8-a5f2-11f1-980b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-30T193523Z-1134131169-RC259NAMFZV1-RTRMADP-3-NIGER-SECURITY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e85749a2-a5e5-11f1-991f-530b91485ab7</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 10:51:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Tunisia's iconic Sidi Bou Said town added to UNESCO world heritage list</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tunisia-s-iconic-sidi-bou-said-town-added-to-unesco-world-heritage-list</link><description>
In Tunisia, UNESCO recognised the town of Sidi Bou Said as a world heritage site this July. The designation marks a new period in the cultural preservation of this historic tourist site. The special status may help as it battles erosion, like in the floods this last January, but it will also help boost its lesser known Sufi mystical traditions. FRANCE 24's Lilia Blaise and Hamdi Tlili were there to report on the Kharja ceremonies, which run in the town from mid-august til the end of September.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e0762b4-a5ec-11f1-b2ed-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9848547386a96a33b66a998-82826885.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e0762b4-a5ec-11f1-b2ed-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9848547386a96a33b66a998-82826885.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2bd67f5a-a5e5-11f1-81ed-530b91485ab7</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 10:07:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Kenyan airport staff strike delays thousands of passengers</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/kenya-airport-staff-strike-delays-thousands-of-passengers</link><description>
In tonight's edition: A workers' strike at Kenya's main airport leaves travellers grounded. Also, Ghanaian cocoa farmers are ramping up their pushback against a new law preventing them from using their land for anything else without permission. And in Tunisia, the picturesque town of Sidi Bou Saïd has been recognised by UNESCO as being important to global heritage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/96d6a118-a5e0-11f1-a0cb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-13511471166a968f280732b9-02561987.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/96d6a118-a5e0-11f1-a0cb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-13511471166a968f280732b9-02561987.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">37ba1456-a579-11f1-9c74-fb7aabece8fd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 20:20:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Niger junta puts down mutiny with help from Russia's Africa Corps</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260830-niger-junta-aided-by-russian-paramilitary-forces-regains-control-after-mutiny</link><description>
Life returned to normal in Niger's capital on Sunday, a day after mutineers stormed both the presidential palace and a military base at Niamey's main airport, resisting forces loyal to the ruling junta until Russia’s Africa Corps intervened. State TV reported that dozens of soldiers were killed or arrested, with some paraded in front of cameras live on television.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/907628b0-93b2-11f1-80c8-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26169614751820-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/907628b0-93b2-11f1-80c8-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26169614751820-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e6b792ce-a481-11f1-b478-51393a6e9b38</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 15:20:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/907628b0-93b2-11f1-80c8-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26169614751820-1.jpg">© AP file photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Niger: Junta says back in control after mutiny</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/niger-junta-says-back-in-control-after-mutiny</link><description>
Gunfire and explosions have been reported in Niger, as mutinying soldiers attempted to storm the presidential palace in the capital, Niamey, in a challenge to the ruling junta. The government said it had regained control after hours of fighting on Saturday. Léo Paichard and Nick Rushworth report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6de5a756-a44e-11f1-bda9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Niger-Junta.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6de5a756-a44e-11f1-bda9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Niger-Junta.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">91657b78-a44b-11f1-b67e-ef30ccbee3a0</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 08:41:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Niger's junta says 'regaining control' after clashes in capital</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/niger-s-junta-says-regaining-control-after-clashes-in-capital</link><description>
Niger's ​defense ​ministry said the armed forces were ​progressively ‌retaking ⁠control ‌of sites targeted in ⁠an overnight attack on ​the ‌capital Niamey, according to a ‌statement read ​on state television, which resumed broadcasting ​on ​Saturday after ​temporarily going ​offline.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f4cff7f8-a3a4-11f1-a6e7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-140055-140232-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f4cff7f8-a3a4-11f1-a6e7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-140055-140232-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fa522b7e-a3a4-11f1-88ea-f30ef7d965b0</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 12:33:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Niger junta regains control after mutiny with help from Russian paramilitary forces</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260829-gunfire-and-explosions-heard-near-military-base-in-niger-s-capital</link><description>
Niger's junta said Saturday it was back in control after mutineers held soldiers hostage at a military base next to the capital's airport. Russian Africa Corps paramilitary forces helped members of Niger's presidential guard recapture the air base, killing some of the mutineers, according to diplomatic and security sources. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51c3eb72-6ae8-11f1-ac04-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-94JQ3CU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51c3eb72-6ae8-11f1-ac04-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-94JQ3CU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fb448536-a36d-11f1-bb59-513a32e153e1</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 06:33:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51c3eb72-6ae8-11f1-ac04-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-94JQ3CU.jpg">© Planet Labs PBC, via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>DR Congo's Tshisekedi calls for national dialogue excluding M23 rebels</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20260828-drc-president-tshisekedi-calls-for-national-dialogue-excluding-m23-rebels</link><description>
In the Democratic Republic of Congo, President Félix Tshisekedi calls for a national dialogue to ease tensions, while excluding M23 rebels from taking part, as the government plans to suspend 11 public universities in rebel-controlled areas.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/57c93cba-a31f-11f1-88eb-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-16681304016a91eff34f8497-63123742.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/57c93cba-a31f-11f1-88eb-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-16681304016a91eff34f8497-63123742.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0cb92712-a31f-11f1-ae58-c51ca87cf5fc</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 20:36:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Clémence WALLER</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Uganda's King of Tooro, once world's youngest reigning monarch, dies at 34</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260828-uganda-s-king-of-tooro-once-world-s-youngest-reigning-monarch-dies-at-34</link><description>
King Oyo Nyimba, leader of the Tooro kingdom in western Uganda, has died at the age of 34, the region's prime minister of his kingdom announced Thursday. Crowned at three years old, he became the world's youngest reigning monarch in 1995.
